From 58b4c7db643f5a6a8d16a9dcb4b9c2d1566fa6da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:51:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(thread): refuse a hole the program ahead has not
 drilled

A thread mill is not centre-cutting and the thread ride feeds it down the
hole's axis. Generate now reads each threaded hole in the stock the
setup's earlier operations leave standing (the drilling laws' prior grid)
over the minor circle less one cell, never narrower than the mill, down
to the mill's lowest point in the hole; stock standing there, or a prior
that cannot be judged, is refused by name. The stamp already digests the
program ahead, so moving the Drill after the Thread marks it Stale.

The thread suites' fixtures move to tests/thread_support and drill the
hole first (modelled to z 4, threaded to z 8); the M8 NC golden gains the
Drill ahead. The Bore ride's axis entry is filed as #1036.

Fixes #992

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
