 thread_mill_rim and coarse_rims threads (#992)

#1005's refresh moved main's #1071 / #1073 thread tests onto a thread
mill; #992's law then refuses each of them for an undrilled hole (the
stock box stands solid where the model's hole is). Each thread now has a
flat end-mill Bore of the same declared holes generated ahead, so the
tests judge the thread's gouge verdict again, not the entry refusal. The
laws are unchanged.

